cabal-version:       3.0
-- Initial package description 'harm.cabal' generated by 'cabal
-- init'.  For further documentation, see
-- http://haskell.org/cabal/users-guide/

description: 
     The harm module provides a CLI interface to process Ars Magica
     characters from JSON or YAML files and produce character sheets in Markdown.

     The JSON/YAML file normally contains a list of advancement stages, and the
     actual state of the character at a given time is computed.

     The libraries are designed with the intention of creating client/server
     systems with different interactive and non-interactive clients.

     The Data.* modules are designed to be generic, while the ArM.*
     modules are specific to Ars Magica.

     For a top down description of the implementation, one should start with
     the `Main` module below.

     ** Inter-dependencies

     The following list covers the modules intended for external use,
     listed in order of dependency, so that no module depends on modules
     further down in the list.  Subdirectories are typically used for 
     internal modules which are expossed via the higher-level modules.

     + Helper modules.  
         + "Data.*" is independent of "ArM.*" 
         + "ArM.Helper" depends only on "Data.*"
         + "ArM.Debug.*" has no dependencies 
     + Data model 
         + "ArM.GameRules" has no dependencies 
         + "ArM.Story" depends only on "ArM.Story.*"
         + "ArM.Trait" depends only on "ArM.Trait.*" and "ArM.Story"
         + "ArM.DB" depends on "ArM.Trait".
           The DB model is not properly used at present.
         + "ArM.Types.Advancement" introduces 'ProtoTrait' and 'Advancement'
         + "ArM.Types.Harm" introduces 'Saga', 'Covenant', and 'Character'
     + Processing
         + "ArM.Processing" includes processes that are common to Character and
           Covenant
         + "ArM.Character" covers operations on characters
         + 'ArM.Covenant" covers operations on Covenants
         + "ArM.Saga" covers 'Saga' level advancement and joint
           advancement of covenants and characters.
     + Formatting and IO
         + 'ArM.Sheet' formats data for output, without choosing an output format
         + 'ArM.Markdown'
         + 'ArM.IO'

     ** Current Status

     The Helper modules are ok at present.  Data.HList and Data.OList could use
     a cleanup, but they are simple and cause little confusion.

     *** Data model

     + ArM.GameRules is very simple and essential, and causes no concern at present.
     + ArM.Story has consistency issues, but they are minor.
     + ArM.Trait and ArM.Types.Advancement could use an internal overhaul,
       but the exposed API is pretty structured and useable.
     + ArM.Types.Harm could possibly use a review of the API

     *** Processing

     ArM.Processing is simple, atomic functions which require no attention at
     the moment.

     The other modules include the advancement process which is not stable at
     the moment.
     + ArM.Saga.Advancement provides the core routines for in-game advancement.
       This has just found a stable structure, which is being extended.
     + ArM.*.InGame have been set up to support ArM.Saga.Advancement.
       This is well-structured and will only grow to support new features.
     + ArM.Character.CharGen has been cleaned up and is fairly well-structured.
     + ArM.Character.Inference is ok; it exports only one functions which has been
       documented.
     
     Other routines is a mesh of new and old code.

     *** Formatting and IO

     + "ArM.Markdown" is a mess, but it should only be reviewed when the
       main data model is better organised.
     + "ArM.Sheet" is probably OK, but may be reviewed in conjunction with
       the above.
     + "ArM.IO" is pretty well-structured and causes no concern.






name:                harm
version:             0.1.0
